# Snippet of lmnopGAME plot?????? I don't even know this isn't near finished
#
# The game starts in lmnopTOWN, the first destination of the protagonist's journey
# from their hometown. They are trying to obtain the VAD medication for their terminally ill father,
# and must travel a far distance.
#
# They have been hearing a commanding voice, but they have been able to ignore it until thus far (this
# is the canon reason as to why the player gains control over the protagonist).
#
# The way through lmnopTOWN is blocked by a puzzle (see the script for lmnopTOWN).
#
# The NPCs hold clues to help solve the puzzle to progress through lmnopTOWN.
#
# In the N-route, the player forces the protagonist to talk to the NPCs.
#
# In the D-route, the player *tries* to force the protagonost to fight some or all of the NPCs. As # they
# are 1) unarmed and 2) do not repeatedly try to force it, no NPCs can be killed. The player still
# must solve the puzzle to proceed.
#
# In the S-route, the player must obtain a sword hidden in the Sound building (the building emitting
# the *diegetic* soundtrack music). This is what starts the S-route. From here, they force the
# protagonist to kill each and every NPC (who will not give clues as the protagonist is armed). This
# will take multiple attempts, as the protagonist must be weakened enough to no longer be strong
# enough to fight the voice. The NPCs do not have a chance to fight. After, the player must force the
# protagonist to destroy the puzzle, rather than solve it.
#
# The S-route may be aborted at this point by sparing at least once NPC. The clues from the NPCs
# cannot be obtaibned, as they either fear you are have been killed by you. The only way to get clues
# would be to first talk to the NPCs without the sword, obtain it, kill them (while sparing at least
# one), and then solve the puzzle.
#
# The first NPC you talk to will allude to the placement of the sword by the Sound building if you
# talk to them repeatedly.

zzz 300; # Make lexing sleep for 5 minutes when it sees this

zzz "string"; # If a non-number is used the sum of the text's bytes (up until a semicolon) is used, so it sleeps for 731 seconds here (12 minutes and 11 seconds)
